From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Thief: the sky cubemap drawn every few frames while the sky changes

The game draws one face of its sky anew each frame and its clouds drift, so
the sky cubemap (for the rays: reflections, the light the sky gives) was never
kept and was drawn every frame, about 2 ms of the GPU frame. Drawn every 4th
frame while only its content changes (RTGL1_METAL_SKY_INTERVAL); the view's
own sky is drawn every frame as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0137FfF2kXgpYFjmGxKqakLV
---
--- a/Source/Metal/MetalRasterizer.mm	2026-11-10 15:43:29.135587910 +0100
+++ b/Source/Metal/MetalRasterizer.mm	2026-11-10 15:43:29.186453271 +0100
@@ -957,6 +957,25 @@
             skyCubemapReused = true;
             return true;
         }
+        // Thief RT: a sky that changes every frame -- the game draws one face of its sky anew
+        // each frame, and its clouds drift -- drawn into the cubemap every few frames, not every
+        // frame (2 ms of the GPU's frame, every frame). The cubemap is the sky the rays find
+        // (reflections, the light it gives): a few frames' lag in a drifting cloud is not seen.
+        // The view's own sky is drawn every frame, as before. RTGL1_METAL_SKY_INTERVAL: frames
+        // (4; 1, every change).
+        {
+            static const uint32_t interval = [] {
+                const char* e = std::getenv( "RTGL1_METAL_SKY_INTERVAL" );
+                const int   v = e ? std::atoi( e ) : 4;
+                return uint32_t( v < 1 ? 1 : v > 30 ? 30 : v );
+            }();
+            if( cacheOn && !force && skyCubemapKey != 0 && skyCubemapAge + 1 < interval )
+            {
+                skyCubemapAge++;
+                skyCubemapReused = true;
+                return true;
+            }
+        }
         skyCubemapKey = k;
         skyCubemapAge = 0;
     }
